(@set06_exam_id,'WRITING','BUILD_SENTENCE','Put the words in the correct order to form one grammatical sentence.',NULL,'NONE','["student","the","club","each","a","for","wrote","short","science","summary"]','each student wrote a short summary for the science club',1,'The grammatical order is "each student wrote a short summary for the science club".',105),
(@set06_exam_id,'WRITING','WRITE_EMAIL','You registered for the campus career fair but received a message that the venue has changed. Write an email to the organiser asking for the new location and confirming whether your online workshop sign-up still holds. Aim for roughly fifty to seventy words and include a suitable greeting and closing.',NULL,'NONE',NULL,NULL,0,'A strong answer greets the organiser, asks for the new venue, checks whether the workshop booking still applies, and closes politely.',106),
(@set06_exam_id,'WRITING','WRITE_EMAIL','You borrowed a reference book from the writing centre and it is now overdue, but you had emailed a renewal request that the desk missed. Write an email to the centre explaining the situation and asking them not to charge a late fee. Aim for fifty to eighty words and give a clear subject line.',NULL,'NONE',NULL,NULL,0,'A strong answer states the overdue book, notes the earlier renewal email, apologises, and asks politely that the fee be waived.',107),
(@set06_exam_id,'WRITING','WRITE_DISCUSSION','Your university is deciding whether all students must take one public-speaking course before graduating. One student says it builds a skill nearly everyone needs at work; another says it wastes time for students who will never speak in public. Write your own opinion, giving at least one reason and a concrete example. Aim for seventy to one hundred words.',NULL,'NONE',NULL,NULL,0,'A strong answer states a clear position, develops it with a reason and a specific example, and responds to the two student viewpoints.',108),
(@set06_exam_id,'WRITING','WRITE_DISCUSSION','A campus committee is choosing whether to extend the library into the night or to open earlier in the morning. Kelly prefers all-night access before deadlines, while Marco argues that an early start better suits students who sleep at night. Write your own view with a reason and a supporting detail. Aim for seventy to one hundred words.',NULL,'NONE',NULL,NULL,0,'A strong answer picks one option or a balanced plan, supports it with a reason and detail, and engages the two students'' points.',109);
